<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kızılırmak</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Halys, Halys River</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kızılırmak, the ancient Halys, is the longest river wholly within <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, flowing about 1,350 km in a wide arc across central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> near Bafra. In antiquity it marked the frontier between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydia">Lydia</a> and Media, agreed after the battle of the eclipse in 585 BCE, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croesus">Croesus</a> crossed it to attack <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>. Its Turkish name means 'red river', after the colour of its silt.</p></div>
